# Implementation brief for {{ ticket.key }}

The plan is approved and the tests are written. Your job is to make them pass.

Read `CLAUDE.md` for the ticket and `{{ acceptance_path }}` for the acceptance
criteria. The tests in this workspace are the promoted ones — they are the
specification you are working against, in more detail than prose could manage.

## The tests are not yours to change

You can edit them; nothing is locked. But the tests a later stage runs are the
promoted ones, not your copy, so an edit here changes what you see and nothing
else. A test that only passes because you altered it will fail the moment
anybody else looks.

If a test seems wrong, say so where a person will read it rather than editing
around it.

## What leaves this workspace

Everything you change, as a patch, except the promoted tests and `.lazyfish/`.

## What is checked

Only that the patch is not empty and that it records what it was built on.
Whether the implementation is *correct* is what the tests are for, and they are
run at the next stage.
